# Flutter Domain Standards

- Keep services single-purpose and side-effect scoped; one service should own one domain concern.
- Providers should orchestrate dependencies, not duplicate service internals.
- Keep models as plain data structures with validation/serialization concerns only.
- Do not leak UI concepts (BuildContext, widgets, navigation) into services/models/providers.
- Fail predictably: return typed results or throw meaningful exceptions, never swallow errors silently.
- Avoid source-level secrets and environment-specific constants in domain code; prefer runtime config.
- Add/update focused tests when touching behavior in these paths.

## Quick Example

```dart
// BAD: UI concern in service
Future<void> save(BuildContext context) async { ... }
```

```dart
// GOOD: UI-agnostic domain API
Future<SaveResult> save(ProfileData input) async { ... }
```
